@startuml Manifest Status

' ADR 0004, decisions P6 and X3. As built (plan 15).
' The manifest is the Administrator's sign-off of one vehicle's load, plus the document pack generated
' from the load and its declarations. Cargo, ferry, declarations and delivery state live elsewhere:
' see docs/states/ for the box, convoy, truck-list entry and declaration lifecycles.
'
' The earlier ten-state model (Created ... Returned) is in git history at commit f659eed.

title Manifest status: the load sign-off
caption ADR 0004; decisions P6, X3. Implemented by plan 15.

state "Proposed" as Proposed : the load is ready for sign-off
state "Approved" as Approved : an Administrator has vouched\nfor the vehicle's load
state "Rejected" as Rejected : sent back to be fixed

[*] --> Proposed : opened on the truck-list entry\n[truck list published]
Proposed --> Approved : Administrator approves
Proposed --> Rejected : Administrator rejects
Rejected --> Proposed : load fixed, proposed again
Approved --> Proposed : the load changed\n(re-approval needed, X3; written by\nthe load change, never requested)

note right of Approved
  Approval files nothing. Declarations are
  prepared after sign-off, and filing is a
  separate act (ADR 0006).
  The freeze applies to the declared snapshot,
  not to the load: allocating, moving or removing
  a box, replacing a box, or a box that is seized,
  lost or returned sends the manifest back to
  Proposed in the same transaction.
end note

@enduml
